GRANT 1: the custos gate and its DeModFrame codec, LGPL-3.0-only
-----------------------------------------------------------------

DeMoD LLC additionally licenses each file listed below, and every earlier
version of it published in this repository, under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 3 only (LGPL-3.0-only). A recipient may use a listed
file under LGPL-3.0-only or under GPL-3.0-or-later, as they choose.

  tests/conformance/entry23_demodframe_golden_vectors.exsc
  tests/conformance/entry23/codex.exsc
  examples/custos/custos.exsc

The grant covers works compiled from the listed files, including the C that
`exsc --emitte c` emits from them, so far as those works are based on the
listed files. What the compiler itself contributes to compiled output is
covered separately, by Exception A in LICENSE.EXCEPTION.

Why: DeMoD's dcf-ws-bridge and demod-remote-bridge link custos.gen.c, the C
that exsc emits from these three files, and ship it under LGPL-3.0-only
(github.com/ALH477/DeMoD, web/bridge/custos/PROVENANCE.md). Exception A
releases compiled output from the licence of the compiler, not from the
licence of the program compiled; this grant supplies the second permission.
Punctim's exsecutor/ directory carries copies of the codec under the same
terms, granted in each copy's header.

Every other file in this repository keeps the terms in LICENSE and
LICENSE.EXCEPTION, and no other file is relicensed by implication.
